id: pm-pdr8t1
title: "The merge-safety gate verifies one history stream of 2,058 and never checks drift, so a clean merge that provably corrupts stream anchoring passes CI green"
description: "ci.yml's tracker merge-safety step runs validate --check-storage-integrity (not --check-history-drift) and verifies the hash chain of a single newest-created item. A two-branch merge reproduced on 2026-07-26 exits git merge 0, produces a correct merged item, and leaves the stream with verify_failed:current_item_hash_mismatch — detectable by --check-history-drift, invisible to the gate as written. Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched merge/history-verify/CI-gate items across all statuses; pm-9j2r3b owns the cause, pm-kpftft owns the validate/health warning ratchet, pm-c0wthb owns fence-fails-open, pm-76dnfg owns randomized merge properties. No item covers the gate's sampling."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:ci",ci-gate,durability,history,integrity,merge-safety,multi-agent
created_at: "2026-07-26T05:41:52.203Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T00:06:10.391Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T00:05:39.108Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The merge-safety CI step verifies every history stream in the workspace rather than a representative, using pm validate --check-history-drift with workspace-wide strict-exit semantics on the pull-request path; a drifted, missing, unreadable, or chain-mismatched stream anywhere fails the build; a single deep pm history --verify --strict-exit call is retained and explicitly named as a command smoke test, not as the coverage; a negative-control fixture workspace containing one deliberately drifted stream proves the gate fails, per pm-k6t4yb; the gate's enablement is sequenced behind pm-9j2r3b or lands together with post-merge reconcile wiring, so the invariant is true before it is enforced; the step's name and output state the number of streams verified so coverage can never silently shrink again"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Workspace-wide history integrity is enforced on the pull-request path instead of sampled at 0.05 percent
value: A merge wave that drifts hundreds of streams fails CI instead of shipping; the immutability claim becomes continuously proven rather than periodically asserted
why_now: "Reproduced live on 2026-07-26: a conflict-free field-aware merge leaves the workspace failing its own pm validate --check-history-drift, and the CI step named merge-safety would not have seen it"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "The static gate now installs merge drivers with extensions disabled, rejects any resulting .gitattributes diff, and runs all-stream validation plus the representative command smoke in the same deterministic runtime."
expected_result: "A fresh CI clone bootstraps its clone-local merge drivers, proves the committed extension-independent fence is reproducible, and strictly verifies every tracker history stream plus storage integrity."
actual_result: The first PR head verified every history stream but failed because the ephemeral clone had no Git driver configuration and the committed fence contained ten patterns contributed only by a developer-local runtime.
